==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|ang}} ''[[hræfter]]''.

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# In time to come; in some future time or state.
#* Dryden:
#*: '''Hereafter''' he from war shall come.

====Translations====
* Dutch: [[hierna]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# A future existence or state.
#* Addison:
#*: 'Tis Heaven itself that points out an '''hereafter'''.

====Synonyms====
* [[afterlife]]

